.policy "ruff-n812-lowercase-imported-as-non-lowercase" revision 2
.description "Keep the alias of an imported lowercase name lowercase; an uppercase alias makes readers mistake a function or module for a class or constant."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N812 (pep8-naming): a lowercase name imported under an alias with an uppercase letter. Exempt when the
// name or the alias matches `pep8-naming.ignore-names`.
//   from mod import lowercase as Lowercase    ← N812
//   import os.path as osp                      not reported
#include "python/naming.rr"

.violation N812(at: node, x: symbol, a: symbol) code "N812"
    "Use a lowercase alias instead of `{a}` for `{x}` and update its uses; leave it if `{x}` is really a class or constant despite its lowercase name."
    suppress ruff "N812"
N812(i, x, a) :- alias_import(i, x, a), cased_lower(x), !lower_name(a), !naming_ignored(x), !naming_ignored(a).
